@startuml BikeSystemArchitecture
title Bike Theft Prediction System - Software Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam nodesep 15
skinparam ranksep 25

' NARROW VERTICAL LAYOUT - Single Column for Word Document Width
' HARDWARE COMPONENTS
node "Client Hardware" as CH
component "Web Browser" as Browser
component "React Frontend" as React
node "Server Hardware" as SH  
component "Flask API" as Flask
component "Python Runtime" as Python
component "Authentication" as Auth
component "Session Manager" as Session
component "Data Validator" as Validator
component "File System" as FileSystem
component "CatBoost Model v1" as ML1
component "CatBoost Model v2" as ML2
component "MongoDB Driver" as MongoDriver
node "Database Hardware" as DH
database "MongoDB Atlas" as MongoDB
database "Local Storage" as LocalDB
component "Gmail SMTP" as SMTP
cloud "Gmail Cloud" as GmailCloud
cloud "MongoDB Cloud" as MongoCloud

' Force single column vertical layout
CH -[hidden]down-> Browser
Browser -[hidden]down-> React
React -[hidden]down-> SH
SH -[hidden]down-> Flask
Flask -[hidden]down-> Python
Python -[hidden]down-> Auth
Auth -[hidden]down-> Session
Session -[hidden]down-> Validator
Validator -[hidden]down-> FileSystem
FileSystem -[hidden]down-> ML1
ML1 -[hidden]down-> ML2
ML2 -[hidden]down-> MongoDriver
MongoDriver -[hidden]down-> DH
DH -[hidden]down-> MongoDB
MongoDB -[hidden]down-> LocalDB
LocalDB -[hidden]down-> SMTP
SMTP -[hidden]down-> GmailCloud
GmailCloud -[hidden]down-> MongoCloud

' COMPREHENSIVE DATA FLOW WITH PROPER LABELS
CH --> Browser : "1. User Access via HTTP/HTTPS"
Browser --> React : "2. Load React Application"  
React --> Flask : "3. JSON API Request"
Flask --> Python : "4. Execute Python Code"
Python --> Auth : "5. Authenticate User"
Auth --> Session : "6. Create/Manage Session"
Session --> Validator : "7. Validate Input Data"
Validator --> ML1 : "8a. Process with CatBoost v1"
Validator --> ML2 : "8b. Process with CatBoost v2"
ML1 --> MongoDriver : "9a. Store ML Results v1"
ML2 --> MongoDriver : "9b. Store ML Results v2"
MongoDriver --> MongoDB : "10. Save to Cloud Database"
MongoDriver --> LocalDB : "11. Cache Locally"
MongoDB --> MongoCloud : "12. Cloud Synchronization"
Flask --> SMTP : "13. Send Email Notification"
SMTP --> GmailCloud : "14. Gmail Service Integration"
Flask --> React : "15. Return JSON Response"
React --> Browser : "16. Display Results to User"

' SEPARATE DOCUMENTATION BOXES - NOT CONNECTED TO MAIN DIAGRAM
note as HardwareDoc
**HARDWARE COMPONENT INTERACTION:**
Client Hardware: Desktop/laptop computers and mobile devices with network interfaces
Server Hardware: Web servers with multi-core processors, adequate RAM for ML processing  
Database Hardware: Storage systems with redundant drives, backup systems for data persistence
end note

note as SoftwareDoc
**SOFTWARE COMPONENT COMMUNICATION:**  
React Frontend: Sends JSON requests to Flask API endpoints, handles user interactions
Flask API: 18 REST endpoints route requests, manage CORS, sessions, authentication
CatBoost Models v1/v2: Process bike theft data using trained ML algorithms
MongoDB Driver: Handles database connections, executes queries, manages data persistence
Gmail SMTP: Sends email notifications using OAuth2 authentication over TLS encryption
end note

note as FlowDoc
**COMPLETE DATA FLOW PROCESS (16 Steps):**
1-2: User accesses system through web browser, React application loads
3-4: Browser sends HTTP requests to Flask API, Python runtime executes logic
5-6: System authenticates user credentials and creates/manages sessions
7-8: Data validator processes input, CatBoost ML models predict recovery probability
9-11: MongoDB Driver stores results in cloud database and local cache
12-14: Data syncs with cloud services, email notifications sent via Gmail SMTP
15-16: Flask returns JSON response to React frontend, results displayed to user
end note

legend bottom right
**COMPREHENSIVE LEGEND:**
Node = Hardware Component | Component = Software Module
Database = Data Storage | Cloud = External Service  
Arrow = Data Flow Direction | Numbers (1-16) = Processing Sequence

**TECHNOLOGY STACK:**
Frontend: React.js, HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript
Backend: Python Flask, CatBoost ML, Authentication
Database: MongoDB Atlas, Local File Storage  
External: Gmail SMTP, OAuth2, TLS/HTTPS
Hardware: Client devices, Web servers, Database servers
end legend

@enduml